"text": "In 1739, Britain went to war with Spain over a single ear. Captain Robert Jenkins said Spanish coast guards had cut it off eight years earlier. Nobody cared. Then he told Parliament. Crowds roared. The Prime Minister didn't even want a war, but the crowd won. Wait, all that over an ear? You see, the ear was just an excuse. The real fight was over trade and smuggling. Even the name came later. A historian made it up over a century after. History forgot the trade deals. It remembered the ear.",
